-- Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems (Fees) Regulations, 5785-2025
-- תקנות הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר (אגרות), התשפ"ה-2025
-- Made under ss.59 and 60 of the Law. Kovetz HaTakanot 5785 p. 2116 (issue 11951); signed
-- 6 July 2025, published 9 July 2025, in force 16 July 2025 (reg. 5).
-- Amended by Kovetz HaTakanot 12383 of 4 May 2026, 5786 p. 2062 (signed 28 April
-- 2026 by Yariv Levin), which defined the theoretical examination, inserted
-- reg. 2(a1) for it and moved the appeal fee onto it.
--
-- THE TWO ENACTED TEXTS SIT ON L4'S RULE-EFFECTIVE-TIME AXIS. There is one rule
-- for regulation 2, `the fee prescribed for`, and it reads `RULES EFFECTIVE
-- DATE` -- the ambient "which version of the law applies" axis -- to decide
-- which of the two texts it is reading. A caller asks the SAME question of a
-- different vintage of the law by pinning that axis with
-- `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT`; see the Illustrations at the foot of this
-- file. Three regimes, two boundaries:
--   * before 16 July 2025  -- the Regulations were not yet in force, so NOTHING
--                             is prescribed for any service. Not "no fee was
--                             payable under a rule"; no rule yet existed.
--   * 16 July 2025 onward  -- the text as made (KT 11951, 5785 p. 2116).
--   * 4 May 2026 onward    -- the text as amended (KT 12383, 5786 p. 2062).
-- The boundaries are inclusive: the fee on the commencement day itself is the
-- new one. See `the day the Regulations came into force` and
-- `the day the 5786 amendment came into force` for how each date is established.
--
-- THE SIMPLEX DRAFT IS DELIBERATELY NOT ON THAT AXIS. It is encoded separately,
-- as `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` and its companions, and those
-- rules take no date and read no axis. That is the point, not an omission: the
-- rule-effective-time axis is indexed by COMMENCEMENT, and a draft has no
-- commencement. It was never in force, so there is no day on which asking "what
-- did the law say?" could correctly return the draft's answers. A draft and a
-- version of an instrument are different kinds of object: a version is a point
-- on the timeline of an instrument, a draft is a counterfactual about it. Put
-- the draft on the axis and you would have to invent a date it never had, and
-- the encoding would then assert -- silently, and falsely -- that on some real
-- day the theoretical examination cost 273 shekels. It never did.
--
-- Regulations 3 (indexation), 4 (payment as a precondition) and 5
-- (commencement) are encoded ONCE and shared by both: they did not change, and
-- the draft's text of them is the text that was made.
@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `Chapter A -- Definitions`
§§ `reg. 1 Definitions`

-- "בחינה עיונית" -- the theoretical examination; "בחינה מעשית" -- the practical
-- examination: the two halves of the examination the Division of Vocational
-- Training sets for the completion certificate under s.2 of the Law.
-- reg. 1 as made defined only the practical examination. The 5786 amendment's
-- reg. 1 inserted the theoretical one after it; that insertion is what makes
-- the new head in reg. 2(a1) legible, and it moves on the same axis as reg. 2.
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `theoretical examination`
    `practical examination`
    `appeal against a theoretical examination score`
    `appeal against a practical examination score`
    `application for a licence`                 -- the draft's head: "בעד בקשה לקבלת רישיון או לחידושו", s.5 of the Law
    `receipt or renewal of a licence`           -- the head as made: "בעד קבלת רישיון או חידושו", s.5 of the Law
    `temporary licence for a foreign expert`    -- application or renewal under s.9 of the Law

§ `The two points on the rule-effective-time axis`

-- The commencement of the principal Regulations is not asserted here; it is
-- COMPUTED, by reg. 5 itself, from the day of publication. reg. 5 is therefore
-- load-bearing rather than decorative: change its seven days and the axis
-- boundary moves with it.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day the Regulations came into force` @nlg the day the Fees Regulations came into force, seven days after their publication on 9 July 2025
                                                @nlg:he יום תחילתן של תקנות האגרות, שבעה ימים מיום פרסומן ב־9 ביולי 2025
    IS `the Regulations commence on` (YMD 2025 7 9)

-- ESTABLISHED, not guessed -- and established by a route worth stating, because
-- the amending instrument does not state it itself.
--
-- The amending regulations, תקנות הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג
-- אוויר (אגרות) (תיקון), התשפ"ו-2026, Kovetz HaTakanot 12383 of י"ז באייר
-- התשפ"ו (4 May 2026), 5786 p. 2062, were read in full from the gazette issue
-- itself (olaw.org.il/takanot/takanot-12383.pdf, two pages). They contain
-- exactly two operative regulations -- reg. 1, amending reg. 1 of the principal
-- Regulations to insert the definition of "בחינה עיונית"; reg. 2, amending
-- reg. 2 to insert (a1) and to rewrite (b) -- followed by the signature of
-- Yariv Levin, Minister of Labour, dated י"א באייר התשפ"ו (28 April 2026), and
-- three footnote citations. THERE IS NO תחילה (commencement) PROVISION AT ALL.
--
-- Silence is not a gap here; it is the trigger for a default. Section 17 of the
-- Interpretation Ordinance [New Version], פקודת הפרשנות [נוסח חדש], provides:
-- "תקנות בנות־פעל תחיקתי יפורסמו ברשומות, ותחילת תקפן ביום פרסומן, אם אין
-- הוראה אחרת בענין זה" -- regulations of a legislative character shall be
-- published in Reshumot, and their commencement is the day of their
-- publication, unless there is another provision in the matter. There is none,
-- so the amendment commenced on its day of publication, 4 May 2026. (Section 21
-- of the Interpretation Law, 5741-1981 fixes the hour at 00:01 of that day;
-- this encoding works in whole days and does not model the hour.)
--
-- Note what this does NOT mean: reg. 5 of the principal Regulations, "seven
-- days from publication", does not reach the amending instrument. reg. 5 fixed
-- the commencement of the Regulations it belongs to, an event that had already
-- happened in July 2025; the amending regulations are a separate חיקוק with
-- their own commencement. The alternative reading -- that an amendment which
-- writes text INTO the principal Regulations rides that instrument's own
-- commencement rule and so began on 11 May 2026 -- is recorded and rejected as
-- fork F6 in NOTES.md section 4.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day the 5786 amendment came into force` @nlg the day the 5786 amendment came into force, the day it was published in Kovetz HaTakanot 12383
                                                   @nlg:he יום תחילתו של תיקון התשפ"ו, יום פרסומו בקובץ התקנות 12383
    IS YMD 2026 5 4

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Regulations are in force` @nlg the Fees Regulations are in force under the version of the law being applied
                                     @nlg:he תקנות האגרות עומדות בתוקפן לפי נוסח הדין החל
    IF (DATE_SERIAL `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`) AT LEAST (DATE_SERIAL `the day the Regulations came into force`)

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 5786 amendment is in force` @nlg the 5786 amendment is in force under the version of the law being applied
                                       @nlg:he תיקון התשפ"ו עומד בתוקפו לפי נוסח הדין החל
    IF (DATE_SERIAL `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`) AT LEAST (DATE_SERIAL `the day the 5786 amendment came into force`)

§ `Chapter B -- Fees`
§§ `reg. 2 Fees -- the text as made, Kovetz HaTakanot 5785 p. 2116`

-- Read from the gazette issue, Kovetz HaTakanot 11951 of 9 July 2025, p. 2116:
-- (a) for a practical examination, the candidate shall pay a fee of 194 new shekels;
-- (b) where an appeal is lodged against THE examination score, the appellant
--     shall pay, in addition to the fee under subregulation (a), 40 new shekels
--     per appeal;
-- (c) for the RECEIPT or renewal of a licence under s.5 of the Law, 284 new shekels
--     -- the word "בקשה" (application) of the draft is gone: the fee now falls
--     due when the licence issues, and a refused applicant owes nothing (F5);
-- (d) for an application for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its
--     renewal, under s.9 of the Law, 398 new shekels.
-- Regulation 1 as made defined only "בחינה מעשית", the practical examination, so
-- "the examination" in (b) can only be that one, and (b) says so itself by
-- pointing at (a). The theoretical examination appears nowhere in the text as
-- made: no fee, and no appeal fee.
GIVEN service IS A Service
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the fee prescribed by reg. 2 as made for` @nlg the fee the text of regulation 2 as made in July 2025 prescribes for %service%, in new shekels, if any
                                                 @nlg:he האגרה שנוסח תקנה 2 כנוסחה עם התקנתה ביולי 2025 קובע בעד %service%, בשקלים חדשים, אם נקבעה
    IS CONSIDER service
       WHEN `theoretical examination`                    THEN NOTHING    -- no such item
       WHEN `practical examination`                      THEN JUST 194   -- 2(a)
       WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN NOTHING -- no such examination in the text as made
       WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN JUST 40 -- 2(b), "in addition to the fee under (a)"
       WHEN `application for a licence`                  THEN NOTHING    -- no such head as made
       WHEN `receipt or renewal of a licence`            THEN JUST 284   -- 2(c)
       WHEN `temporary licence for a foreign expert`     THEN JUST 398   -- 2(d)

§§ `reg. 2 Fees -- the text as amended, Kovetz HaTakanot 5786 p. 2062`

-- The amendment added a definition of "בחינה עיונית" to reg. 1, inserted
-- (a1) -- for a theoretical examination, 158 new shekels --
-- and rewrote (b): the appeal fee now attaches to the THEORETICAL examination
-- score, "in addition to the fee under (a1)". So the appeal fee moved from the
-- practical examination to the theoretical one. Everything else as made, and
-- the OTHERWISE below says exactly that: an amendment changes the items it
-- names and leaves the rest of the instrument standing.
GIVEN service IS A Service
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the fee prescribed by reg. 2 as amended for` @nlg the fee the text of regulation 2 as amended in 5786 prescribes for %service%, in new shekels, if any
                                                    @nlg:he האגרה שנוסח תקנה 2 כנוסחה לאחר תיקון התשפ"ו קובע בעד %service%, בשקלים חדשים, אם נקבעה
    IS CONSIDER service
       WHEN `theoretical examination`                        THEN JUST 158  -- 2(a1)
       WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN JUST 40   -- 2(b) as amended
       WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN NOTHING   -- 2(b) as amended reaches the theoretical score only
       OTHERWISE `the fee prescribed by reg. 2 as made for` service

§§ `reg. 2 Fees -- the one rule, on the rule-effective-time axis`

-- ONE rule for regulation 2. It takes no vintage argument; it reads
-- `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` -- the ambient rule-effective-time axis -- and answers
-- as the text in force on that day answers. Callers pin the axis with
-- `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT <date>`; with nothing pinned, L4's fallback
-- chain is explicit rule-version pin, then the valid-time pin, then today.
-- That default is the presumption against retroactivity: ask about a fact that
-- happened in 2025 and you get the 2025 law without having to say so.
@export The fee, in new shekels, that the Fees Regulations prescribe for a service under the version of the text in force on the rule-effective date; NOTHING means no fee is prescribed -- which, before 16 July 2025, is because the Regulations did not yet exist
GIVEN service IS A Service  @desc the service the fee is charged for
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the fee prescribed for` @nlg the fee prescribed for %service% by the Fees Regulations as they stood on the rule-effective date
                               @nlg:he האגרה הקבועה בעד %service% בתקנות האגרות כנוסחן ביום החל על הדין
    IS IF `the 5786 amendment is in force`
       THEN `the fee prescribed by reg. 2 as amended for` service
       ELSE IF `the Regulations are in force`
            THEN `the fee prescribed by reg. 2 as made for` service
            ELSE NOTHING   -- before 16 July 2025: no fee is prescribed, because no such rule was yet in force

§§ `reg. 2 -- what an appellant must tender in all`

-- Both enacted texts make the appeal fee payable "in addition to" an
-- examination fee, and they disagree about WHICH. As made, 2(b) points at (a),
-- the practical fee: 234. As amended, 2(b) points at (a1), the theoretical fee:
-- 198. Before commencement neither exists, and the ELSE branch then answers
-- NOTHING of its own accord, because `the fee prescribed for` does.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the examination fee the appeal fee is added to` @nlg the examination fee the appeal fee is charged in addition to, under the text in force on the rule-effective date
                                                       @nlg:he אגרת הבחינה שאגרת ההשגה נוספת עליה, לפי הנוסח שבתוקף ביום החל על הדין
    IS IF `the 5786 amendment is in force`
       THEN `the fee prescribed for` `theoretical examination`   -- 2(b) as amended: "בתקנת משנה (א1)"
       ELSE `the fee prescribed for` `practical examination`     -- 2(b) as made: "בתקנת משנה (א)"

GIVEN appeal IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      base   IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the appeal fee plus its base` @nlg the appeal fee %appeal%, plus the examination fee %base% it is charged in addition to
                                     @nlg:he אגרת ההשגה %appeal%, בתוספת אגרת הבחינה %base% שהיא נוספת עליה
    IS CONSIDER appeal
       WHEN NOTHING     THEN NOTHING
       WHEN JUST charge THEN CONSIDER base
                             WHEN NOTHING   THEN JUST charge
                             WHEN JUST under THEN JUST (charge PLUS under)

@export The whole amount an applicant must tender for a service under the Fees Regulations as they stood on the rule-effective date: for an appeal, the appeal fee plus the examination fee it is charged in addition to; for anything else, the fee itself; NOTHING where neither is priced
GIVEN service IS A Service  @desc the service applied for
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the total to be tendered for` @nlg the total to be tendered for %service% under the Fees Regulations as they stood on the rule-effective date
                                     @nlg:he הסכום הכולל שיש לשלם בעד %service% לפי תקנות האגרות כנוסחן ביום החל על הדין
    IS CONSIDER service
       WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN `the appeal fee plus its base` (`the fee prescribed for` service) `the examination fee the appeal fee is added to`
       WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN `the appeal fee plus its base` (`the fee prescribed for` service) `the examination fee the appeal fee is added to`
       OTHERWISE `the fee prescribed for` service

§ `The SimpLEX draft -- a counterfactual, OFF the time axis`

-- Figure 4 of Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov & Gelbard, "When Computers Speak Laws"
-- (Law, Society & Culture 8, 2025) is a screen capture of the Israeli Ministry
-- of Justice's SimpLEX drafting-and-testing tool, showing the DRAFT of these
-- Regulations. It reads, in translation:
--   (a) for a theoretical examination, a fee of 273 new shekels;
--   (b) for a practical examination, a fee of 194 new shekels;
--   (c) where an appeal is lodged against the result of a theoretical or a
--       practical examination, 40 new shekels per appeal, in addition to the
--       fee under (a);
--   (d) for an APPLICATION to receive or renew a licence under s.5 of the Law,
--       284 new shekels -- charged on the application, so a refused applicant
--       has paid (fork F5 in NOTES.md; s.59 of the Law lists the application
--       and the grant as separate fee heads);
--   (e) for an application for a temporary licence for a foreign expert under
--       "s.8 of the Law" [sic -- s.9 in the bill and the Act], 398 new shekels.
--
-- NOTHING BELOW READS `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`, and nothing below can be reached
-- by `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT`. There is no date at which these rules are
-- the law, so there is no date at which to ask for them. They are reached by
-- name, and the name says what they are. Every rule here is a statement in the
-- subjunctive -- what the draft WOULD have required -- and the naming keeps it
-- that way at every call site.
GIVEN service IS A Service  @desc the service the fee is charged for
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
@export The fee, in new shekels, the never-enacted SimpLEX draft of regulation 2 prescribed for a service; a counterfactual, not a version of the law -- it has no commencement date and sits on no time axis
DECIDE `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` @nlg the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for %service%, in new shekels, if any
                                                 @nlg:he האגרה שהטיוטה שבצילום המסך קובעת בעד %service%, בשקלים חדשים, אם נקבעה
    IS CONSIDER service
       WHEN `theoretical examination`                    THEN JUST 273   -- draft 2(a)
       WHEN `practical examination`                      THEN JUST 194   -- draft 2(b)
       WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN JUST 40 -- draft 2(c)
       WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN JUST 40 -- draft 2(c)
       WHEN `application for a licence`                  THEN JUST 284   -- draft 2(d)
       WHEN `receipt or renewal of a licence`            THEN NOTHING    -- the draft prices the application, not the receipt
       WHEN `temporary licence for a foreign expert`     THEN JUST 398   -- draft 2(e)

-- The draft's 2(c) covers an appeal on EITHER examination but adds the 40 to
-- "the fee under (a)", which in the draft is the THEORETICAL fee, 273 -- so read
-- literally a practical-examination appellant tenders 313, not 194 + 40 (fork
-- F5). SimpLEX's own row 7, "appeal with payment (40)", is silent on the
-- aggregate, so the draft's reading of it is underdetermined on its own text.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the examination fee the draft's appeal fee is added to` @nlg the examination fee the draft's appeal fee is charged in addition to
                                                               @nlg:he אגרת הבחינה שאגרת ההשגה שבטיוטה נוספת עליה
    IS `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` `theoretical examination`  -- draft 2(c): "the fee under (a)" = 2(a), the theoretical one (F5)

@export The whole amount the never-enacted SimpLEX draft would have required for a service: for an appeal, the appeal fee plus the fee under the draft's 2(a); for anything else, the fee itself
GIVEN service IS A Service  @desc the service applied for
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the total the SimpLEX draft would have required for` @nlg the total the SimpLEX draft would have required for %service%
                                                            @nlg:he הסכום הכולל שהטיוטה הייתה דורשת בעד %service%
    IS CONSIDER service
       WHEN `appeal against a theoretical examination score` THEN `the appeal fee plus its base` (`the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` service) `the examination fee the draft's appeal fee is added to`
       WHEN `appeal against a practical examination score`   THEN `the appeal fee plus its base` (`the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` service) `the examination fee the draft's appeal fee is added to`
       OTHERWISE `the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` service

§ `Chapter B continued -- the provisions that did not change`

§§ `reg. 3 Updating of fees`

-- (a) The fee amounts in reg. 2 are updated on 1 January of each year (the
--     update day) by the rate of change of the new index against the base
--     index, and rounded to the nearest whole new shekel; for this purpose --
--     "the new index": the index published in the November before the update day;
--     "the base index": the index published in the November before the previous
--     update day, and for the first update day after these Regulations commence,
--     the index published in the month before they commenced;
--     "index": the consumer price index published by the Central Bureau of Statistics.
-- Rounding at exactly one half is not settled by the text; half-up is adopted
-- (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest whole shekel` x MEANS FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)

@export A fee amount after the annual 1 January update under regulation 3: scaled by the consumer price index and rounded to the nearest whole new shekel
GIVEN fee IS A NUMBER          @desc the fee amount before the update, in new shekels
      `new index` IS A NUMBER  @desc the CPI published in the November before the update day
      `base index` IS A NUMBER @desc the CPI published in the November before the previous update day (or the month before commencement, for the first update)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the updated fee` @nlg the fee of %fee% shekels updated by the ratio of the index %`new index`% to the base index %`base index`%, rounded to the nearest shekel
                        @nlg:he האגרה בסך %fee% שקלים חדשים מעודכנת לפי שיעור השינוי של המדד החדש %`new index`% לעומת המדד היסודי %`base index`%, ומעוגלת לשקל החדש השלם הקרוב
    IS `rounded to the nearest whole shekel` (fee TIMES `new index` DIVIDED BY `base index`)

§§ `reg. 4 Payment of the fee as a condition of a licence or an examination`

-- The registrar shall not grant or renew a licence for which a fee is prescribed,
-- and the Division shall not allow the examinations or an appeal for which a fee
-- is prescribed, unless the applicant has paid that fee in full.
-- Where NO fee is prescribed for the service, reg. 4 has nothing to bite on.
-- The appeal fee is "in addition to" the examination fee: the appellant's total
-- outlay is 198 as amended, of which 158 bought the examination. `paid` here is
-- the amount paid toward the fee for THIS service, so an appeal is 40; the
-- aggregate is `the total to be tendered for`, above, and reg. 4's "in full"
-- is read against the service's own fee, not the aggregate (fork F5).
-- reg. 3(b), the Director-General's duty to publish the updated reg. 2 in
-- Reshumot, is not modelled.
--
-- reg. 4 is encoded ONCE, as a function of whatever fee is prescribed. Both the
-- enacted rule below and the draft's counterfactual feed it, which is faithful:
-- the draft's reg. 4 is word for word the reg. 4 that was made.
GIVEN `fee prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc the fee prescribed for the service, or NOTHING where none is
      paid             IS A NUMBER       @desc the amount the applicant has paid toward that fee, in new shekels
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `regulation 4 is satisfied` @nlg regulation 4 is satisfied where the fee prescribed is %`fee prescribed`% and %paid% shekels have been paid
                                  @nlg:he תקנה 4 מתקיימת כאשר האגרה הקבועה היא %`fee prescribed`% ושולמו %paid% שקלים חדשים
    IF CONSIDER `fee prescribed`
       WHEN NOTHING  THEN TRUE
       WHEN JUST fee THEN paid AT LEAST fee

@export Whether the registrar or the Division of Vocational Training may provide a service, given what the applicant has paid, under regulation 4 and the text of regulation 2 in force on the rule-effective date
GIVEN service IS A Service  @desc the service applied for
      paid    IS A NUMBER   @desc the amount the applicant has paid toward the fee, in new shekels
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service may be provided` @nlg %service% may be provided to an applicant who has paid %paid% shekels, under the Fees Regulations as they stood on the rule-effective date
                                    @nlg:he ניתן לתת את %service% למבקש הרישיון או השירות ששילם %paid% שקלים חדשים, לפי תקנות האגרות כנוסחן ביום החל על הדין
    IF `regulation 4 is satisfied` (`the fee prescribed for` service) paid

@export Whether the never-enacted SimpLEX draft would have allowed the service on the amount paid; a counterfactual, on no time axis
GIVEN service IS A Service  @desc the service applied for
      paid    IS A NUMBER   @desc the amount the applicant has paid toward the fee, in new shekels
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the SimpLEX draft would have allowed` @nlg the SimpLEX draft would have allowed %service% to an applicant who has paid %paid% shekels
                                             @nlg:he הטיוטה הייתה מתירה את %service% למבקש ששילם %paid% שקלים חדשים
    IF `regulation 4 is satisfied` (`the fee the SimpLEX draft prescribes for` service) paid

§§ `reg. 5 Commencement`

GIVEN published IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the Regulations commence on` @nlg the Regulations commence seven days after their publication on %published%
                                    @nlg:he תחילתן של התקנות שבעה ימים מיום פרסומן ביום %published%
    IS published PLUS 7

§ `Illustrations -- one rule, three vintages of the law`

-- THE DEMONSTRATION. The same question, asked of three different vintages of
-- the same instrument, answered by ONE rule. Nothing about the rule's
-- definition changes between these lines; only the date the axis is pinned to.

-- What must an appellant against a PRACTICAL examination score tender in all?
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 7 1)  (`the total to be tendered for` `appeal against a practical examination score`)   -- NOTHING: not yet in force
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 7 16) (`the total to be tendered for` `appeal against a practical examination score`)   -- JUST 234: 194 + 40
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 5 4)  (`the total to be tendered for` `appeal against a practical examination score`)   -- NOTHING: the appeal fee moved

-- And against a THEORETICAL examination score -- the mirror image.
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 7 1)  (`the total to be tendered for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`) -- NOTHING: not yet in force
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 7 16) (`the total to be tendered for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`) -- NOTHING: no such examination as made
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 5 4)  (`the total to be tendered for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score`) -- JUST 198: 158 + 40

-- The counterfactual takes no date, because there is no date to take.
#EVAL `the total the SimpLEX draft would have required for` `appeal against a practical examination score`   -- JUST 313
#EVAL `the total the SimpLEX draft would have required for` `appeal against a theoretical examination score` -- JUST 313

§§ `The same, as assertions`

